# ============================================================
# What must stay OUT of the build context
# ============================================================
#
# Before Docker runs a single instruction it copies this whole folder
# to the daemon - the "build context". Without this file that copy is
# 484 MB, of which 473 MB is .venv, and you wait for it on EVERY build.
#
# .venv is also actively harmful, not just slow: it holds Windows
# binaries that are useless inside a Linux container, and if it were
# copied over /app it would shadow the packages pip just installed.
.venv/
venv/
env/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc

# Created by a shell redirect accident.
$null

# Secrets never belong in an image. Anyone who can pull the image can
# read every layer, including files you deleted in a later layer.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.env

.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Docs do not affect how the app runs.
README.md
*.md

# ============================================================
# What IS copied, deliberately
# ============================================================
#
# sample_data/ stays in - all 10.2 MB. It is the app's data source,
# not a cache. An image without it starts cleanly and fails on the
# first page that reads a table.
#
# tests/ stays in too, so you can run the smoke test INSIDE the
# container:
#
#   docker run --rm urban-company-app python tests/smoke_test.py
#
# That is a stronger check than running it on your laptop - it tests
# the environment that actually ships.
